`append_partitioned(storage, additions)` accepts two dictionaries mapping non-empty string partition names to lists of records. It returns a new dictionary where records from `additions` are appended to records already present in the same partition. Existing partition order is retained; new partitions appear afterward in their order from `additions`. Record order is preserved. Empty dictionaries are valid.

Both dictionaries, all record lists, and every nested record value must be deeply isolated from the result. Mutating either input or the result later must not affect the others. Neither input may be mutated. Non-dictionaries, invalid keys, or non-list record collections raise `TypeError` or `ValueError` as appropriate.

